{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/13184-c-c-tfv-and-vampires","id":13184,"title":"C&C: TFV and Vampires","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-17T22:14:33-08:00","id":13184,"title":"C&C: TFV and Vampires","content":"I don't see why TFV even need Vampires, American Black Ops (in this case very very black) are many things, but underfunded they aren't. Even if they can't get it that way, there's plenty of accounting tricks the government could use to fund the TFV, $50000 for a light bulb for example. Last but not least, they could 'accidently' lose it, like they <a href=\"http://www.theguardian.com/world/2007/feb/08/usa.iraq1\" target=\"_blank\">lost $12bn dollars in Iraq.</a><br /> <br /> It just seems like an incredibly bad thought out idea for no real reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1072,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1072-theye1","user":"theye1","date":". 11-18-2013, 01:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1072-theye1","name":"theye1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1072_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-17T22:34:11-08:00","id":13194,"title":"","content":"Thematically the reason is to draw on the idea of the &quot;hard men of hard decisions&quot; compromising themselves with one enemy for the greater good against other enemies. Because shadows behind the curtain that would horrify the good guys carrying out the missions is part of the genre that TF: VALKYRIE plays off of.<br /> <br /> In-setting, to enjoy the full budgetary power of US black ops, they would need to part of the established chain of command and answer to the Joint Chiefs, if not the President. I don't believe HtV assumes that is the case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-17T23:32:18-08:00","id":13216,"title":"","content":"I choose to ignore the vampire funding in favor of donations from Cheiron in exchange for access to remains of monsters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T00:23:06-08:00","id":13234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/13184-c-c-tfv-and-vampires?p=13194#post13194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thematically the reason is to draw on the idea of the &quot;hard men of hard decisions&quot; compromising themselves with one enemy for the greater good against other enemies.Because shadows behind the curtain that would horrify the good guys carrying out the missions is part of the genre that TF: VALKYRIE plays off of.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except the TFV are now totally presented as either unwitting pawns of Vampires, or in some cases active patsies for the Vampires, C&amp;C basically says that the TFV's Vampire backers control the day-to-day mission of the TFV. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/13184-c-c-tfv-and-vampires?p=13194#post13194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">In-setting, to enjoy the full budgetary power of US black ops, they would need to part of the established chain of command and answer to the Joint Chiefs, if not the President. I don't believe HtV assumes that is the case.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>Hunter the Vigil says that the TFV was founded by the Joint Chiefs of Staff, without the presidents knowledge. <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> <br /> <br /> <br /> </span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1072-theye1","name":"theye1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1072_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T01:05:12-08:00","id":13247,"title":"","content":"Yeah, C&amp;C handled it badly. It works a lot better if you go with how Night Stalkers implies it works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T01:35:34-08:00","id":13262,"title":"","content":"I agree that the vampires bit seems pretty poorly implemented; but I don't think it's that big an issue. The only time it'll come up is if you're running a campaign dedicated to it.<br /> <br /> On a side note, Seers of the Throne offers the titbit that much of the technology that TFV makes use of is indeed funded and created by the normal R&amp;D budget of the US. Why have a separate R&amp;D budget when you can just take the stuff paid for by DARPA?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T01:52:56-08:00","id":13270,"title":"","content":"What on earth is everyone talking about? Due to writer illnes and a hard deadline C&amp;C was published with every core group except Task Force: VALKYRIE. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/13184-c-c-tfv-and-vampires?p=13194#post13194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thematically the reason is to draw on the idea of the &quot;hard men of hard decisions&quot; compromising themselves with one enemy for the greater good against other enemies. Because shadows behind the curtain that would horrify the good guys carrying out the missions is part of the genre that TF: VALKYRIE plays off of.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually don't think that works as an explanation. In fact putting non-Abraham Vampire's in charge of VALKYRIE actually moves them away from being the thematic hard men. It shifts the blame from the hunters to the vampires.<br /> <br /> With the vampires TF:V make only one hard decision, to accept the bribe. Every time they leave a horrific vampire alive that's not a new hard decision but a repercussion of the old one. Without it then every time they decide that a vampire is doing a good enough job keeping the Kindred orderly that you have to leave it alive that's a new hard choice.<br /> <br /> Besides, with the thematic niche of being the military group they should answer to the joint chiefs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T04:44:35-08:00","id":13324,"title":"","content":"You can always have them be vampires dedicated to the genocide of their own race, but balancing that out with wanting to avoid the chaos that occurs when you disrupt the standard vampire power structure (Reap the Whirlwind's SAS shows what happens when the Prince just up and dies).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T08:38:13-08:00","id":13409,"title":"","content":"They could be pawns of whoever controls VII...that could be kind of neat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/961-chewygranola","name":"ChewyGranola","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"254"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T08:49:00-08:00","id":13415,"title":"","content":"You can disagree with the decision, but it was a thoroughly thought-out one.<br /> <br /> Here's the origin of the decision, courtesy of the person who wrote that segment (&quot;Tier_Three&quot;): <a href=\"http://forums.white-wolf.com/default.aspx?g=posts&amp;m=586448#post586448\" target=\"_blank\">http://forums.white-wolf.com/default...448#post586448</a><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">I saw the way the story went in </span></span></span><i>Night Stalkers</i><span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">, when I was advised to at least hint that the vampires were running the show.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">I originally wrote the thing out as being a kind of a story, connecting Malleus Maleficarum and VALKYRIE through the mists of time.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Welcome to the first Cold War in human history. Two mighty forces battling it out behind the shadows, wielding unthinkable powers, and the soul of the entire world is at stake.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Before there even was a United States, when the only world was the Old World, the Church and the remnants of the dying Camarilla were at each other's throats.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Then the Church hunters began attacking with Benedictions. And these were </span></span></span><i>very</i><span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"> effective against the Kindred.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">In fact, had the New World not been discovered, the Malleus might have managed to do something unthinkable - reduce a monstrous species to extinction.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Nonetheless, with the opening of the new trade routes across the Atlantic, the Kindred managed to flee the worst ministrations of Mother Church, ensuring the species' survival. But the war had another effect.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">When Padre Ambrogio unlocked the secrets of Benedictions, and the Malleus began to score some real victories against the Kindred (they claim Milan as one of their victories; to this day The Lucifuge sits on her throne, chortling as she remembers their conceit back then - and now) the vampires realised that they could no longer feed openly against mortals.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">The rise of Malleus Maleficarum brought about the current Tradition of The Masquerade among the Kindred. The hunters were responsible for why vampires have to work in the shadows and behind the scenes.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">And then there was the New World, and the Renaissance and Enlightenment back home. Science and Reason began flexing its muscles after a long slumber wedged under the Church's glutes. A new kind of civilisation began to appear in the Americas, and a new breed of hunter conspiracy. Imagine an 1800s TF:V with electricity, vacuum tube computers and radios poached from their British equivalent - who had radio fifty years before Marconi, and RADAR in 1900.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">The Brits gave VALKYRIE the radios. They didn't give them RADAR.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Now imagine the most astute Kindred of the time, realising that a momentous opportunity had arisen. The Cold War had not ended, but it was about to shift from one major player to the other. From the Malleus - locked away in Europe amid increasingly stifling obsolescence in a world changing faster than they could keep up - to VALKYRIE, in the forefront of that changing world. Riding the wave.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">How better to keep the new player under control than by getting in at its inception before it could get too strong? They wouldn't be able to stop VALKYRIE doing its thing - VALKYRIE's too big even for the Kindred to control completely - but they could run a form of damage limitation and stop the Kindred's most critical assets from getting killed, or even noticed, by the VALKYRIE war machine.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Individuals may come and go, and VALKYRIE will still be able to claim major victories, but they would never be able to exterminate the Kindred.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">I'm going to add another pointer to help you lot out, if you're still worried about the whole &quot;vampires running TF:V&quot; thing.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Look at my writeup in </span></span></span><i>Night Stalkers</i><span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">. There's a whole project in there that Stearne haven't even thought of suborning. They're focused way too much on keeping Project: TWILIGHT under their thumb; and Project: ADAMSKI's too busy playing catchup with the vampires who have their own, very efficient form of Masquerade (and ADAMSKI are just finding this out </span></span></span><i>now</i><span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"> ...)</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">So who does that leave? Oh, yes. Underfunded, ignored, chasing lights in the sky, Bigfoot sightings, cattle mutilations and black helicopters. Or is that a cover, using some cunning ADAMSKI subterfuge and misdirection?</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Go. Look it up. Then ask yourselves what those boys at Project: FORT could </span></span></span><i>really</i><span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"> be up to.</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":508,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/508-sikker","user":"sikker","date":". 11-18-2013, 11:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/508-sikker","name":"sikker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar508_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T09:40:15-08:00","id":13447,"title":"","content":"Thanks for that sikker, I never saw the authors side of the story before.<br /> <br /> <br /> I think that when theye1 said &quot;bad thought out idea&quot; he meant that it was a bad conclusion, not that it hadn't been thought through. At least that's how I'm familiar with the idiom he used.<br /> <br /> <br /> Now that aside. As good as it was to see the authors point of view... I still think it's a terrible idea.<br /> <br /> First of all, nothing in there answers the key question: Why does it reinforce TF:V's core theme, government run military hunters.<br /> <br /> <br /> Secondly, it just seems poorly thought out. This secret history of the vampire kind world ignores... well the rise of Anglicism, the existence of entire Eastern Othordox Church and the subcontinent of India for starters. There's no way that the MM alone would push vampire's to extinction.<br /> <br /> <br /> Thirdly it is, at lest it gives a very strong impression of, depending on this story to be interesting. Certainly a lot of people didn't find the idea of TF:V vampire overlords interesting, and when the author tried to explain why it's interesting he went straight to this story and nothing else. This story is not in any of the books. Depending on a story that doesn't exist in your head is just bad design. This one is mostly a presentation issue, but if you don't have the word count to make the big reveal more interesting than &quot;guess what? Vampires!&quot;, it's by far better not to do it at all.<br /> <br /> <br /> Still though. It's point #1 that's the real issue in my book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 11-18-2013, 12:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T09:50:47-08:00","id":13454,"title":"","content":"I think Task Force Valkyrie being backed by vampires is a good decision for two reasons:<br /> <br /> 1) TFV is a conspiracy in the most UFO enthusiast sense of the word. They're literally the men in black. Having them be controlled by the masters of conspiracy* and undying bureaucracy reinforces their theme of being enigmatic, probably corrupt, black ops conspirators.<br /> 2) Considering the emphasis on vampires being good at controlling mortals and their systems, on the ageless webs of intrigue they are supposed to spin, I for one applaud that this is, for once, actually reflected in the setting. As much as it's a clich\u00e9 to say &quot;vampires are secretly in control!&quot; in popular media, Vampire: the Requiem has not actually been shown in control of anything of consequence throughout its run. Vampires should secretly control *something*, and TFV fits the bill better than anything else available.<br /> <br /> *=At least until Demon arrived.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/508-sikker","name":"sikker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar508_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T10:01:59-08:00","id":13463,"title":"","content":"This doesn't make them any more enigmatic, it makes them far less enigmatic and corrupt. The enigma and corruption is transferred from TF:V to the Vampires. Since this is a hunter game that's the opposite to how it should be. (Also, if you're going to have an enigmatic organization, you need a better reveal than Vampires!)<br /> <br /> <br /> On the second point. This is a hunter game not a vampire game. If vampires should be in charge of something important (I think they shouldn't) it should be in a vampire book not a hunter book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T10:04:24-08:00","id":13465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/13184-c-c-tfv-and-vampires?p=13463#post13463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This doesn't make them any more enigmatic, it makes them far less enigmatic and corrupt. The enigma and corruption is transferred from TF:V to the Vampires. Since this is a hunter game that's the opposite to how it should be. (Also, if you're going to have an enigmatic organization, you need a better reveal than Vampires!)</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree in every possible way. Let's leave it at that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/508-sikker","name":"sikker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar508_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T16:27:35-08:00","id":13682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>sikker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/13184-c-c-tfv-and-vampires?p=13415#post13415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can disagree with the decision, but it was a thoroughly thought-out one.<br /> <br /> Here's the origin of the decision, courtesy of the person who wrote that segment (&quot;Tier_Three&quot;):</div> </div> </div> </div>You can't see that TFV being controlled day-to-day by vampires deprotagonizes the TFV? Secondly, a story that literally has no evidence in the books, and contradicted in Requiem for Rome books, who which out the origins of the traditions fairly well. It's also a little eurocentric, ignoring areas that weren't majority catholic.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>sikker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/13184-c-c-tfv-and-vampires?p=13415#post13415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">TFV is a conspiracy in the most UFO enthusiast sense of the word. They're literally the men in black. Having them be controlled by the masters of conspiracy* and undying bureaucracy reinforces their theme of being enigmatic, probably corrupt, black ops conspirators.<br /> 2) Considering the emphasis on vampires being good at controlling mortals and their systems, on the ageless webs of intrigue they are supposed to spin, I for one applaud that this is, for once, actually reflected in the setting. As much as it's a clich\u00e9 to say &quot;vampires are secretly in control!&quot; in popular media, Vampire: the Requiem has not actually been shown in control of anything of consequence throughout its run. Vampires should secretly control *something*, and TFV fits the bill better than anything else available.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where's is it enigmatic? There's no mystery; Vampires are in fairly tight control of the TFV. Secondly, it contradicts what we know about Vampire influence in the American government. Nightstalkers indicates while Vampires may control a senator or two, they certainly don't have the pull to co-opt the USA's hunter programme. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1072-theye1","name":"theye1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1072_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T17:02:10-08:00","id":13694,"title":"","content":"They still kill vampires, they still kill other supernatural threats. It leaves what the vampires behind it exactly want up to the ST. The Lucifuge aren't deprotagonized by getting their powers from hell and having their mentor be some weird immortal mystery woman.<br /> The enigma comes when what does the individual vampire or vampire cabal behind it wants. Maybe it's En Isiratuu returned to bring another 12,000 year rule over all of vampire kind. Maybe it's a bunch of America's founding fathers, turned to vampires, leaving themselves a foothold. Maybe it's the VII, maybe it's a democratic union of 50 vampires who vote on everything. Maybe it's the Endiku ensuring that they always have more vampires to spawn with. I can understand you being upset if it said 'TFV is run by John the Vampire who wants to rule all of humanity,' but there's nothing like that. There's a vampire, or vampires behind it, and they occasionally let vampires off the hook.<br /> <br /> As for Nightstalkers, I think you're misquoting, it actually says the Barrett Commission has a senator or two. It's the hunters who don't have the pull.<br /> <br /> All that said, I can certainly understand why people might not want to run it that way. It seems to hearken back to Vampire the Masquerade for me, where vampires were behind everything, but to be fair vampires do have a lot of abilities to control minds and crowds and bind people to them, so it does make sense that at least some vampires would have power beyond their domain and covenant. Being the toolbox that it is, however, you are free not to run it like that. It doesn't affect anything if you take it out. You can easily play Task Force Valkyrie as not having any vampires behind it, just like you can have every conspiracy run by vampires behind the scenes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T17:08:42-08:00","id":13697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>theye1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/13184-c-c-tfv-and-vampires?p=13682#post13682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">contradicted in Requiem for Rome books, who which out the origins of the traditions fairly well</div> </div> </div> </div>Did we read the same RfR? Because the only one of the three Traditions of the Camarilla that matches the modern Traditions is the taboo against diablerie.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-19T00:29:30-08:00","id":13828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/13184-c-c-tfv-and-vampires?p=13697#post13697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did we read the same RfR? Because the only one of the three Traditions of the Camarilla that matches the modern Traditions is the taboo against diablerie.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fall of Rome, pg 198, talks about how the seeds of the modern traditions were founded in Byzantium.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1072-theye1","name":"theye1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1072_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-19T04:30:34-08:00","id":13929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/13184-c-c-tfv-and-vampires?p=13694#post13694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Lucifuge aren't deprotagonized by getting their powers from hell and having their mentor be some weird immortal mystery woman.</div> </div> </div> </div>Deprotagonised is a hard thing to pin down, but there is a few fundamental difference between the Lucifgue and TF:V<br /> <br /> 1) Lady Lucifuge is a part of the Lucifuge, the Vampires are outside TF:V. <br /> <br /> 2) The Lucifuge's major goals (protecting humanity and preventing it's members from becoming evil) are probably shared and supported by Lady Lucifuge. She probably created them. In contrast TF:V thinks their major is protecting humanity from monsters but in fact it is protecting vampires from humanity. Protecting the Masquerade, a campaign against other monster hunters.<br /> <br /> (Having powers from hell doesn't matter here nor there. It's what you do with said powers and what you had to do to get them that matters).<br /> <br /> <br /> Deprotagonising is a very hard concept to nail down in general. However I would say that the way this moves TF:V's ability to decide their own goals to the vampires is at least a little deprotagonising (for the organisation as a whole).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/13184-c-c-tfv-and-vampires?p=13694#post13694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The enigma comes when what does the individual vampire or vampire cabal behind it wants.</div> </div> </div> </div> Which is a terrible place to put the enigma. The enigma should come from the hunters, not the monsters.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/13184-c-c-tfv-and-vampires?p=13694#post13694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It doesn't affect anything if you take it out. You can easily play Task Force Valkyrie as not having any vampires behind it, just like you can have every conspiracy run by vampires behind the scenes.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a fallacy. Everyone here knows that you can ignore it, I suspect most of us do. However we're talking about the books. What we do in our own games doesn't have any affect on how good or how bad the books are and obviously the writers should try and create good material that people don't want to ignore.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-19T10:03:32-08:00","id":14142,"title":"","content":"I'm actually quite a fan of vampires being behind one of the larger hunter organizations. And it has very little impact on the individual corruption considering its only a handful of people with status 5 (not even all of them) that know about it. Its funding and a few odd rules. Who is to say it isn't VII doing it as a way to annihilate other vampires? The whole &quot;seemingly insurmountable tide of enemies&quot; certainly seems to indicate that it isn't just any covenant or group.<br /> <br /> Does it stop them from killing vampires? For the most part no, it does not, only in cases that its some ally of the group funding them do they do that. VII operates much like terrorist cells, sometimes even doing reprogramming of other vampires. I don't know about you, but that seems awfully appropriate for a group that MIGHT be behind TF:V. The individual corruption, and even that at middle tiers and even upper tiers is primarily not influenced by it.<br /> <br /> They influence the missions, but if only a handful of high status individuals know, they can't influence ALL the missions most likely. Otherwise the mentioned mistakes wouldn't happen at all. Funding with a few extra &quot;Kill these vampires instead of these.&quot; is hardly as impacting as you seem to make it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-19T10:17:03-08:00","id":14147,"title":"","content":"Hunter counts being suborned by monsters as one of the big threats of the Vigil - one of the major core-book groups being so suborned (the Lucifuge and <span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#404040\">Ambrogio </span></span></span>don't count as they're both committed to the Vigil) gives that danger teeth. And unlike the rumoured supernatural secret at the core of Cheiron, this is a cancering that PC's could theoretically eradicate without fundamentally changing or eliminating TFV.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-19T13:16:04-08:00","id":14245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rani Neferet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/13184-c-c-tfv-and-vampires?p=14142#post14142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They influence the missions, but if only a handful of high status individuals know, they can't influence ALL the missions most likely. Otherwise the mentioned mistakes wouldn't happen at all. Funding with a few extra &quot;Kill these vampires instead of these.&quot; is hardly as impacting as you seem to make it.</div> </div> </div> </div>To me it sounds like you're saying it's not so bad because I can ignore it. If the best you say in it's favour is ignore it, it doesn't convince me that it's a great idea.<br /> <br /> I don't think it's VII though. I think it would be rare for VII to ever say let that vampire live.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/13184-c-c-tfv-and-vampires?p=14147#post14147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hunter counts being suborned by monsters as one of the big threats of the Vigil - one of the major core-book groups being so suborned (the Lucifuge and <span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#404040\">Ambrogio </span></span></span>don't count as they're both committed to the Vigil) gives that danger teeth.</div> </div> </div> </div>This idea that having a subsumed group to illustrate the damgers of the vigil is not a bad one, but it was still handled badly.<br /> <br /> Firstly because the idea of military hunters is too thematically important to also be the subsumed group. Instead they should have created something unique that doesn't lock down a major media archetype for monster hunters as the subsumed group.<br /> <br /> Secodly because it's not part of the core. The subsumed group should say right up front to players that these people are unknowingly pawns of the monsters. TF:V only hinted at it and never had the reveal until 7 books in. That's not a good way to handle it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-20T06:02:09-08:00","id":14663,"title":"","content":"I think something we forgot about is the need for black funding. Vampire money doesn't even show up on a senate subcommittee for this stuff, the $850,000 talked about in C&amp;C is just to keep it government in the first place. It makes perfect sense when you consider some vampires have money enough to do this, and that they definitely have enemies. Plus, TFV's mission is to conceal everything. Vampires want to conceal everything. It doesn't mean TFV is blindly subservient to the vampires and their orders either. Example, how do we know that STERNE isn't supposed to allow hunters knowledge of what's going on so that they can slowly get out of vampire control? Plus, it's been said in more than a few books that the bureaucratic hangups mean that a hard-charging TFV cell can easily eliminate a few vampires before command comes down on them for it.<br /> <br /> Also, TFV might not want to be under complete government control, because face it, the US government doesn't know half the time what half of it's agencies are doing. We've seen the ATF give guns to criminals, the CIA running drug rings, the military testing germ warfare on US civilians, and the FBI and NSA observing everything. TFV and the vampires to me represent just another example of the government's agencies not following their own rules because to them it needs to be done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-20T08:32:43-08:00","id":14718,"title":"","content":"To me having vampires control TFV fits in with what I've always seen as an underdeveloped possibility, vampire monster hunters. After all the Masquerade depends on a lot being hidden and while vampires are generally willing and able to clean up after themselves, what about all those other random things? Vampires arguably have a far stronger interest in killing the supernatural than hunters, a hunter may want to save those he knows or the people hurt by the supernatural but a vampire is hunting things that if exposed could destroy his entire species. And given vampires tendancy to get things done by manipulating mortals controlling the governments response to the supernatural seems a natural fit. <br /> <br /> While its still corruption I see it from the perspective of the interests of Hunters and Vampires lining up pretty well. Vampires want the supernatural destroyed and hidden with the possible exception of other vampires(and even then they don't usually like each other), hunters want the supernatural destroyed and accept that its going to remain hidden. Its win win for the most part. And where its not win win it can become an interesting struggle between idealism and pragmatism. Will a cell of TFV disobey orders and kill a given vampire? Even if it might mean the end of TFV?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/92-ramza","name":"Ramza","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar92_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-20T09:08:10-08:00","id":14740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flyboy254</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/13184-c-c-tfv-and-vampires?p=14663#post14663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Example, how do we know that STERNE isn't supposed to allow hunters knowledge of what's going on so that they can slowly get out of vampire control?</div> </div> </div> </div> It seems unlikely. If it was, why is certification held on the longest night of the year? That sounds like it's designed to let vampires teach the course or at least observe. The Author's comments do kind of imply that he expects anti-vampire moves to come from FORT or rogue low level agents (PCs, the rogue accountant)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flyboy254</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/13184-c-c-tfv-and-vampires?p=14663#post14663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, TFV might not want to be under complete government control, because face it, the US government doesn't know half the time what half of it's agencies are doing. We've seen the ATF give guns to criminals, the CIA running drug rings, the military testing germ warfare on US civilians, and the FBI and NSA observing everything. TFV and the vampires to me represent just another example of the government's agencies not following their own rules because to them it needs to be done.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I've said above though, I consider that Vampire's detract from this theme. If vampire's are controlling TF:V they do nasty stuff &quot;because vampires&quot;. If vampire's don't control TF:V then TF:V does nasty stuff because they believe it needs to be done.<br /> <br /> That's why I created an alternative where TF:V allied with vampires because of cold war paranoia. American agencies being under foreign control has little precedent, American agencies making terrible alliances that come back to haunt them decades later; well I did intentionally base my version on American - Afghanistan relations.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramza</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/13184-c-c-tfv-and-vampires?p=14718#post14718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To me having vampires control TFV fits in with what I've always seen as an underdeveloped possibility, vampire monster hunters. After all the Masquerade depends on a lot being hidden and while vampires are generally willing and able to clean up after themselves, what about all those other random things? Vampires arguably have a far stronger interest in killing the supernatural than hunters, a hunter may want to save those he knows or the people hurt by the supernatural but a vampire is hunting things that if exposed could destroy his entire species. And given vampires tendancy to get things done by manipulating mortals controlling the governments response to the supernatural seems a natural fit.</div> </div> </div> </div> It is a good fit and I've had vampires working with some of my groups (The Lord Stewards for example) for similar reasons.<br /> <br /> But in a hunter book, for one of the core PC hunter groups, it should be portrayed at worst as cooperation between two groups due to mutual interests rather than vampire's secretly controlling the hunters. Vampire's can secretly control people in their own books, or in the antagonists section of a hunter book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-20T16:43:23-08:00","id":14963,"title":"","content":"The whole idea as presented in C&amp;C never sat right with me. I mean, it's cool and all, and I accept all the reasons why it works and is cool and whatnot, but I can't get fully into it. Reading the writer's justification reinforces that to me, because it feels very oWoD to me. I think having TFV controlled by some tough as nails military guys, written in the same mold as John Marcone from Dresden Files (strong willed enough to accept the supernatural and deal with it) would be my Inner Circle of choice. These guys are making horrible decisions, decisions that maybe make them worse than the monsters they are hunting. I think that speaks to the core themes of Hunter, but then again this is all my opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/961-chewygranola","name":"ChewyGranola","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"254"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-20T17:11:51-08:00","id":14983,"title":"","content":"tl;dr: Some people don't like it, think it's bad. Some people do like it, or don't care.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T16:10:57-08:00","id":16326,"title":"","content":"Don't like it, don't use it? I see value in both interpretations, but don't really care about the realism of a secret government monster killing division.<br /> <br /> There are certain posters who seem to become hyper-obnoxious whenever anybody suggests anything that undermines the conspiracies \u2013 be it in terms of morality or agency \u2013 might be a good thing to put in your horror game. I kind of wish they'd give it a rest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/275-leaper","name":"Leaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar275_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T18:57:30-08:00","id":16408,"title":"","content":"I need the cup in your picture for a friend, Leaper. XD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T23:25:37-08:00","id":17536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>theye1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/13184-c-c-tfv-and-vampires?p=13682#post13682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You can't see that TFV being controlled day-to-day by vampires deprotagonizes the TFV?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;<span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"> VALKYRIE's too big even for the Kindred to control completely - but they could run a form of damage limitation and stop the Kindred's most critical assets from getting killed, or even noticed, by the VALKYRIE war machine.&quot;<br /> <br /> They've corrupted and influence VALKYRIE. They don't control it.<br /> <br /> \u200bThat said, I have an idea for the Stearne Committee that is much more complicated and involves humans still central (if sharing) the driver's seat. It basically comes down VALKYRIE's higher ups having chosen sustainable social order over any &quot;truly free humanity from the horrors of the night&quot; gambits. And so they have CHOSEN to make deals and incorporate the influence of those supernatural factions that seek to preserve the status-quo. So yes, Stearne gets resources and intel from those groups, and in return stears the lower ranked VALKRYIE agents away, and often toward those groups &quot;more dangerous&quot; (read: more transgressive) enemies. Thats how it started, by this point, Seer Thralls and Ghouls are directly involved in Stearne.<br /> <br /> To be clear, this is 100% irrelevant to VALKYRIE protagonism if you don't want to involve it (tons of horrors to honestly fight the good fight against without involving areas Stearne would say &quot;no&quot; to). If you do involve said plot point it is as a reveal to give players a choice to deal with or not.</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 11-25-2013, 02:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T23:32:10-08:00","id":17540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>theye1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/13184-c-c-tfv-and-vampires?p=13682#post13682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Where's is it enigmatic? There's no mystery; Vampires are in fairly tight control of the TFV. Secondly, it contradicts what we know about Vampire influence in the American government. Nightstalkers indicates while Vampires may control a senator or two, they certainly don't have the pull to co-opt the USA's hunter programme.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Only an idiot controls a politician directly. Way too high profile. The power is on K-Street. They don't need Senators, to pull VALKYRIE's strings. They can have the Contractors.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T23:37:58-08:00","id":17545,"title":"","content":"VALKYRIE is even stated to be a multinational joint task force, there's no reason for them to struggle to be funded. If you want them to be forced to morally compromise, have Cheiron funding them instead. Now TF:V still functions the same way it does, but sometimes orders come down the pipe to bring the target in alive or to put up with a corporate consultant/handler on the squad.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T23:46:16-08:00","id":17552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/13184-c-c-tfv-and-vampires?p=17545#post17545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">VALKYRIE is even stated to be a multinational joint task force, there's no reason for them to struggle to be funded. If you want them to be forced to morally compromise, have Cheiron funding them instead. Now TF:V still functions the same way it does, but sometimes orders come down the pipe to bring the target in alive or to put up with a corporate consultant/handler on the squad.</div> </div> </div> </div>Doesn't have the &quot;selling out to the enemy in the name of order&quot; element. I agree the funding excuse doesn't work. I prefer the conscious decision to bring certain supernatural players in &quot;for the greater good&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-25T00:08:22-08:00","id":17571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/13184-c-c-tfv-and-vampires?p=17545#post17545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">VALKYRIE is even stated to be a multinational joint task force.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it borrows manpower from other nations on occasion, but it was formed by the joint chiefs of staff, mandated to protect America from ENEs, and is typically referred to as a government agency, so I'm going to have to disagree here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;These are merely stones...&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/276-merkonan","name":"Merkonan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar276_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-25T02:03:40-08:00","id":17616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/13184-c-c-tfv-and-vampires?p=17552#post17552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Doesn't have the &quot;selling out to the enemy in the name of order&quot; element. I agree the funding excuse doesn't work. I prefer the conscious decision to bring certain supernatural players in &quot;for the greater good&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm agree. Making TF:V aware and giving them a reason to choose to ally with vampires fits the themes better and puts the moral questions where they belong, in the hands of hunters in a way that having vampires subvert TF:V simply does not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-26T05:28:43-08:00","id":18363,"title":"","content":"I think the sidebar would have been well-served by taking the approach the similar one did for Cheiron - presenting several options. For purposes of my games, I tend to rule TFV has a deliberate alliance with both Famous Gil (though they may be unaware of its true nature in that case) and the Invictus. They're not <i>subverted</i>, or even collaborating, per se, they just have other priorities and made shady deals with the &quot;well behaved, pro-establishment&quot; vampires for funding and additional support for national defense operations.<br /> <br /> That is, the Invictus has a phone number it can call when a small, isolated rural town has been overrun by a draugr outbreak. And Task Force: Valkyrie has a number it can call when it needs someone at Guantanamo bay to be Dominated into telling the government what Al Qaeda is up to. There's an obscure line in the VtR corebook about vampires who work for human agencies; I feel like it works both ways. The Invictus finds TFV useful, and TFV finds the Invictus useful. That is, if anything, a little more horrifying than a fully subverted group would be, IMO.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-01T02:22:34-08:00","id":21071,"title":"","content":"They have a big budget, but they also maintain absolute secrecy. A total lack of transparency is not great for a budget of any size in the first place, and almost all of it gets diverted to R&amp;D. In my game, TF:V basically functions as the Shadow IRS. It used to be a secondary function, but the need for funding quickly dominated the agenda.<br /> <br /> So, you've got all of these vampires. The young ones are very likely to be true leeches, able to pull together largish sums of money/other resources if they need to, but those resources are usually not theirs. Not only that, but they have a misplaced sense of pride and bravado, believing that as vampires, they are the true lords of the night. But they aren't, the US government is. These vampires are(usually) fair game, provided that they meet the right criteria. These are the sorts of vampires that most of the low status members of Valkyrie are going to get to know.<br /> <br /> But there are also the old guys. These are the ones with the real power and influence, and most of all, capital. Do you think that they are paying taxes on these considerably large fortunes? When TF:V is in town, you bet your ass they do. To an outsider, it would look very much like Valkyrie has been corrupted by vampires, and their dirty blood money, But as far as Valkyrie sees it, they are the ones who are compromising the vampires, and forcing them to fall in line with the law. The ones who rebel are dealt with quickly, using cutting edge military weapons and tactics.<br /> <br /> Vampires in the know talk a pretty big game of corrupting the government, but they are privately terrified.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><br /> I draw things! Wanna check it out? Click on the link below!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/jordantroy\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/jordantroy</a><br /> <br /> <i><b>YES! I do commissions! </b></i>","edited":{"userid":848,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/848-jtroy","user":"JTroy","date":". 12-01-2013, 05:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/848-jtroy","name":"JTroy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar848_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T09:59:24-08:00","id":21730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JTroy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/13184-c-c-tfv-and-vampires?p=21071#post21071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They have a big budget, but they also maintain absolute secrecy. A total lack of transparency is not great for a budget of any size in the first place, and almost all of it gets diverted to R&amp;D. In my game, TF:V basically functions as the Shadow IRS. It used to be a secondary function, but the need for funding quickly dominated the agenda.<br /> <br /> So, you've got all of these vampires. The young ones are very likely to be true leeches, able to pull together largish sums of money/other resources if they need to, but those resources are usually not theirs. Not only that, but they have a misplaced sense of pride and bravado, believing that as vampires, they are the true lords of the night. But they aren't, the US government is. These vampires are(usually) fair game, provided that they meet the right criteria. These are the sorts of vampires that most of the low status members of Valkyrie are going to get to know.<br /> <br /> But there are also the old guys. These are the ones with the real power and influence, and most of all, capital. Do you think that they are paying taxes on these considerably large fortunes? When TF:V is in town, you bet your ass they do. To an outsider, it would look very much like Valkyrie has been corrupted by vampires, and their dirty blood money, But as far as Valkyrie sees it, they are the ones who are compromising the vampires, and forcing them to fall in line with the law. The ones who rebel are dealt with quickly, using cutting edge military weapons and tactics.<br /> <br /> Vampires in the know talk a pretty big game of corrupting the government, but they are privately terrified.</div> </div> </div> </div>TF:V the Vampire IRS. Interesting take on that. They basically get paid off by people to not hunt them. Of course if the vampires are dead, its difficult for Valkyrie to get at the money, interesting interplay, and could also account for the &quot;Night to night decisions&quot;, given the appropriate pay. One elder might want another elder sacked so pays triple what that elder would normally contribute? I kinda like that thought.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-03T08:44:57-08:00","id":22365,"title":"","content":"Governments are basically insurance companies with armies. If TFV's primary interaction with vampires is, &quot;Nice wealth you've accumulated, shame if anything happened to it...&quot; that's actually kind of hilarious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-03T09:13:35-08:00","id":22375,"title":"","content":"I think that's in danger of moving the Valkyrie too far in the other direction; you're making the kindred so little a threat that they no longer really have any real value for horror. They're a known quantity to be exploited.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-04T16:53:17-08:00","id":23386,"title":"","content":"Well, they're still eating people, and the very government intended to protect those same people is basically taking back taxes to look the other way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-05T17:05:22-08:00","id":24077,"title":"","content":"I get that, my issue is more the way it reduces the Kindred. They're no longer an omnipresent undead menace, they're a population who could be easily rounded up and shot if Valkyrie ever got around to actually doing it's job. It gives the hunters far too much power for my liking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-05T18:27:45-08:00","id":24096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/13184-c-c-tfv-and-vampires?p=24077#post24077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I get that, my issue is more the way it reduces the Kindred. They're no longer an omnipresent undead menace, they're a population who could be easily rounded up and shot if Valkyrie ever got around to actually doing it's job. It gives the hunters far too much power for my liking.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't that sort of the point? THere's a strong reason the monsters haven't taken over the world, and hunters are supposed to be a big part of it.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also I've always thought it strengthens Vampires. Compared to the other, Vampires have always seemed like the most shortchanged, and giving them some of the reigns over a prominent group makes the vampires a stronger mortal threat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 12-05-2013, 09:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-05T22:36:54-08:00","id":24191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/13184-c-c-tfv-and-vampires?p=24096#post24096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't that sort of the point? THere's a strong reason the monsters haven't taken over the world, and hunters are supposed to be a big part of it.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also I've always thought it strengthens Vampires. Compared to the other, Vampires have always seemed like the most shortchanged, and giving them some of the reigns over a prominent group makes the vampires a stronger mortal threat.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do not see how making vampires exist only on the sufferance of a mortal organisation makes them seem like a greater threat in any way whatsoever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T03:03:26-08:00","id":24261,"title":"","content":"Well it's not the existence of vampires. TF:V couldn't drive them to extinction, heck it probably doesn't have any presence in China at all. Rather, vampires keep their penthouses at the sufferance of TF:V and would be forced to hide in basements and attics without millions of dollars worth of money trails pointing to them if they didn't have a deal.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T05:08:11-08:00","id":24297,"title":"","content":"So it's the existence of kindred society that'll be wiped out. You're still removing a large part of the horror.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Isn't that sort of the point? THere's a strong reason the monsters haven't taken over the world, and hunters are supposed to be a big part of it. </div> </div> </div>No. It's declaring Valkyrie the winners if only they could be bothered to do it's job.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T05:18:55-08:00","id":24303,"title":"","content":"Nah, it's not removing horror. This is hunter, not vampires and so the primary horror comes not from the monsters but the toll the Vigil takes upon you. In this TF:V is fitting, the vigil took their morality from them and now they're more interested in the vampire's money than their crimes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T12:55:38-08:00","id":24569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/13184-c-c-tfv-and-vampires?p=24297#post24297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So it's the existence of kindred society that'll be wiped out. You're still removing a large part of the horror.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah. One of the key elements of the World of Darkness is that the horror monsters are really just people stuck in the same situation as real people are - that is, there's no victory, only defeat. You live as long as you can, then you die. You don't save or destroy the world. Things just continue. So most of the monsters have a kind of existential analog with the real world; in this case, vampires are the wealthy class manipulating government to protect their interests, while literally draining the life out of the poor and vulnerable. <br /> <br /> While &quot;the overthrow of humanity by vampires&quot; is a potential source of horror, it's not the kind of horror the WoD is aimed at - it's too disconnected from the real world. Instead we look at the shadows cast by the real world, and darken/deepen them with the supernatural. Vampires never win, and they never lose, because it's not that kind of setting. The line between human interests and vampire interests is too blurred for that kind of binary distinction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T23:54:49-08:00","id":24967,"title":"","content":"It definitely changes the horror that vampires represent, in the way that Conspiracies always do by putting you on more equal footing with the monsters at the price of what-have-you. I took my group from Tier 1, where vampires were ruthless, omnipresent and more often than not an immediate threat to life and limb, into the Tier 3 world where the embattled PC's were suddenly the ones with the power. And they were eager to start abusing that power, just like the vampires had. We get to kick in Dracula's door and shake him down? Damn it feels good to be an Agent.<br /> <br /> But, they also had to evict an ally(in a really unusual twist for this group, everyone loved and wanted to protect this vampire, cute and not particularly threatening as she was) from her haven and serve her the paperwork that would strip her of all of her assets. From there, she watched compliantly, silently crying bloody tears outside as they raided her home and destroyed all of her (ghouled) plants, and shot dead Meatball the Hellhound, a ghoul dog that had saved them on 2 separate occasions in the tier 1 past. They were all pretty fond of Meatball.<br /> <br /> It's a different flavor of horror, but it's definitely still there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><br /> I draw things! Wanna check it out? Click on the link below!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/jordantroy\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/jordantroy</a><br /> <br /> <i><b>YES! I do commissions! </b></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/848-jtroy","name":"JTroy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar848_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}